    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The authors note that the GPT and MLP differ in parameter count, input format, regularization, and learning rate; only one small decoder-only Transformer family and one MLP family are studied. The reported train/test tables are averages across runs but do not give table-level error bars. The paper explicitly says it does not identify the proposed optimization mechanism.",
    "rows_left_out": "No results from other sections were omitted that directly report the fixed- or scaled-budget single-feature k-parity train/test accuracies relevant to the related finding. Results on noisy or multi-feature k-parity were not included because they do not measure delayed generalization after overfitting.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "V1",
        "parts": "No measurement of delayed test-accuracy rise after training saturation, or of the delay versus training-set size; only endpoint accuracies are reported."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "No circuit identification, progress measures or memorisation-removal analysis. A Fourier-gap test is proposed only as future work."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "No non-algorithmic data and no initialisation-scale or weight-norm manipulation."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "No LLM pretraining or fine-tuning on realistic data."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "Weight decay is fixed (1e-3 for GPT, none for MLP) and never varied. No critical dataset size or ungrokking test."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "No comparison of learned algorithms across runs."
      },
      {
        "version": "V7",
        "parts": "Optimiser is held fixed (Adam/AdamW); SGD is explicitly left to future work. No floating-point or softmax analysis."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "Rows are correctly unlinked (versions none, cannot_determine): they are endpoint accuracies, not training-time trajectories. Training and validation curves exist (Figures 13 and 14, N=8000), but the text describes no delayed generalisation in them, so no V1 row can be built. The paper studies the k-parity setting of Barak et al. but does not frame its results as grokking."
